# THE SLUMS, from the ground: the three things that make a city read as a place
# people still live in, under the machines' order (docs/STORY.md §13, how it is
# uncovered). This cited "§8, the quiet region" until the story was rewritten;
# what the frames below prove is about the CITY and did not depend on that arc,
# which is why they are unchanged.
#
#   1. a crowd passes the player and not one head turns
#   2. a machine that passes is walked past unrecognised, and gives itself up
#      only to the slate's read
#   3. one swing in front of that street turns the whole network hostile
#
# Staged on the coast because the city's own landscape file is another builder's
# (`slums/dome`); what is being proved here is the CROWD, the passer and the
# price, none of which is coast-specific. `--folk=30` is the street.
#
#   tools/tour.sh tours/slums_street.tour --seed=4 --village=0 --hour=13 \
#       --weather=clear:0 --folk=30 --give=knife:1 --held=knife

# Nothing of the plan wandering in to confuse what the frames are of.
coast calm
wait 1.0

# --- 1. traffic, not an event -------------------------------------------------
# Everywhere else the player is the most interesting thing to happen all week.
# Here they are one more body going past, and the crowd is the proof.
await crowd_indifferent 6
shot 01-a-street-that-does-not-look-up with folk

walk 1,0 1.2
await crowd_indifferent 6
shot 02-walked-through-and-nobody-turned with folk

# --- 2. one of these is not a person ------------------------------------------
# No lamp, no seam, no violet, and no tag: a body that passes carries none, so
# the picture cannot answer what it is and neither can the player.
spawn passer
wait 1.0
shot 03-one-of-these-is-a-machine with mob:passer,folk

# --- 3. the read is the only way to know --------------------------------------
# Hold the slate on it and the plan says what it is FOR, in its own words.
hold target
await target 5
await testimony 6
await beat:covenant_fed 6
shot 04-the-read-says-what-it-is with mob:passer
release target
wait 0.5

# --- 4. what a street charges for a swing -------------------------------------
# The machines are not hunting anybody here, so violence is not answered with
# violence: it is WITNESSED. One blow in front of thirty people carries a calm
# network past hostile on its own, which is why the swing is almost never the
# right answer in this landscape.
walkto mob 6
press swing
await hit 6
await network_hostile 8
shot 05-one-swing-in-front-of-a-street with mob:passer,folk
